v1.lore = "An unremarkable yet effective rifle, the \'M1886\' has served faithfully as the standard issue infantry rifle for both the Nation and Empire for years, boasting a unique smokeless cartridge and a seven-round internal tube magazine that puts it above the capacities of most other rifles. The ergonomics may leave a lot to be desired, but many look towards the \'M1886\' as the gold standard for any rifle, and it looks to remain a staple of the war for years to come.\n\nYet, it is perhaps better known as the \'Prince\' - being used in the assassination of Prince Leido of the Royal Throne, thus causing the first set of bombs to be dropped on Golden Empire territory. Though the war was already well underway between the two vitriolic factions, it was his death that sent the world below the Surface, rendering it into the barren wasteland it is today.\n\nThe \'Prince\' demonstrated its reliability and accuracy then, as it will for the remainder of the war; and perhaps even longer still."
